{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "./dist",
    // The two Fastify plugins whose *type augmentations* this application's modules
    // write against: `@fastify/rate-limit` adds `rateLimit` to `FastifyContextConfig`
    // (`settings/routes.cache.ts`, `product_feeds/routes.public.ts`) and
    // `@fastify/cookie` adds `setCookie`/`clearCookie` to `FastifyReply` (16 sites in 10
    // modules). Both used to arrive for free: the platform's `http/server.ts`
    // value-imports each and lived under `src/**/*`, so both were in this program. The
    // platform is a package now, and a `.d.ts` carries only the types its own
    // declarations name — neither plugin appears in any of them, and `tsc` elides an
    // unreferenced triple-slash directive from declaration output, so neither the package
    // nor a re-export shim can hand the augmentation on. Naming them here is the
    // application saying which plugins its handlers are written against; a module that
    // starts using a third one adds it, and the failure is a compile error rather than a
    // silence.
    "types": ["node", "@fastify/rate-limit", "@fastify/cookie"]
  },
  // **`scripts/**/*` is in the program, and it was not until 2026-09-12.**
  // A script entered this type-check only when a test happened to import it, so
  // `scripts/acceptance/instance.ts` — which no test imports — was compiled by
  // nothing at all: a `ReferenceError: built is not defined` reached a real
  // acceptance run past a green `pnpm -r run typecheck`, a block-scoped `const`
  // read from outside its block, which is the first thing `tsc` refuses. That is
  // a hole in a gate rather than a bug in a file, and the shape this estate
  // spends its review effort on — a green that means "not looking".
  //
  // It is the type-check's population only. `tsconfig.build.json` overrides
  // `include` with `["src/**/*"]`, so the production image emits exactly what it
  // emitted before, and `lint` names its files on the command line. Measured
  // when it landed: adding the directory surfaced **one** error, in that same
  // unchecked file.
  "include": ["src/**/*", "test/**/*", "scripts/**/*", "vitest*.ts"],
  // **Two programs, not one, since 2026-10-24 (issue #421).** One program over all
  // of the above needed ~2.8 GB of heap and had outgrown its CI cap twice, so
  // `test/contract`, `test/integration` and `test/perf` are type-checked by
  // `test/tsconfig.json` instead — the same compiler options, a separate program.
  // This one keeps `src`, `scripts`, `test/unit` and every shared test helper,
  // and the `vitest*.ts` configurations, which no program read before #421.
  // Both are named in `package.json`'s `typecheck`, and each sits where an
  // editor's nearest-`tsconfig.json` lookup finds it for its own files. The
  // measurements and the choice of two over three are in `.gitlab-ci.yml`'s
  // `quality` job; `workspace-resolution.test.ts` holds every TypeScript file
  // under `backend/` to exactly one of the two, so a directory that falls
  // between them is a red run rather than a file nobody compiles.
  "exclude": ["test/contract/**/*", "test/integration/**/*", "test/perf/**/*"]
}
